WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.912
External Calendars show the events of another calendar inside one of yours, kept

00:00:05.912 --> 00:00:07.568
up to date by the site.

00:00:07.568 --> 00:00:12.080
This video shows how to subscribe a calendar to an iCalendar address, how

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.192
often it is read, what the events look like, and what happens when

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:18.020
an address cannot be used.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.153
Partners, vendors and other teams publish their calendars somewhere else.

00:00:27.153 --> 00:00:32.030
You want to see them next to your own events, without copying anything by hand.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.827
With the External Calendars feature on, a calendar can follow a secret iCalendar

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:43.050
address, such as the one Google Calendar or Outlook shows in a calendar's settings.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.771
The events are copied in, kept up to date, and removed here when

00:00:47.771 --> 00:00:49.416
they are removed there.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:53.500
They cannot be changed here, because the other calendar owns them.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:59.582
Signing in to Google Calendar or Microsoft 365 to keep calendars in step

00:00:59.582 --> 00:01:01.838
both ways is not available.

00:01:01.838 --> 00:01:04.230
The address is the only link.

00:01:08.421 --> 00:01:11.752
Open Manage Calendars, and add a General calendar.

00:01:11.752 --> 00:01:13.477
Name it Partner events.

00:01:13.477 --> 00:01:17.879
Its editor has a Subscription card, with a box to keep this calendar

00:01:17.879 --> 00:01:20.258
in step with an external calendar.

00:01:20.258 --> 00:01:21.091
Tick it.

00:01:21.544 --> 00:01:28.415
Keep the provider on iCalendar address, and paste the external calendar's address.

00:01:28.415 --> 00:01:32.084
It must start with https, http or webcal.

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:37.459
Every sets how often the calendar is read, at least every five minutes.

00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:42.063
The site looks for calendars that are due once every five minutes.

00:01:42.063 --> 00:01:43.214
Choose Save.

00:01:43.665 --> 00:01:47.896
Now try an address that cannot be used, one on this same machine.

00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:52.186
Add another calendar, Broken feed, with a page of this site as its

00:01:52.186 --> 00:01:53.795
address, and save it.

00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:01.022
A few minutes later, the first read has happened.

00:02:01.022 --> 00:02:05.092
Open the Partner events calendar, and look at the Subscription card.

00:02:05.092 --> 00:02:08.777
Last synchronized shows when it last worked, and what it did.

00:02:09.227 --> 00:02:10.650
Open the calendar.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.267
The partner's events are here, in the calendar's color.

00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:15.930
Click an event.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.953
You can read it, but there is no Edit button, because the other calendar owns it.

00:02:20.953 --> 00:02:24.417
Change it there, and it changes here at the next read.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.384
Now the broken feed.

00:02:26.384 --> 00:02:29.185
Its Last synchronized shows why it failed.

00:02:29.185 --> 00:02:33.969
Addresses on the local network cannot be subscribed to, so a calendar cannot

00:02:33.969 --> 00:02:37.178
be used to reach private systems on your network.

00:02:37.629 --> 00:02:42.183
After each failure in a row, the site waits longer before it tries

00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:45.282
again, up to thirty-two times the interval.

00:02:45.282 --> 00:02:51.289
The events already in the calendar stay, and one failing address never blocks the others.

00:02:55.489 --> 00:03:00.764
Use the address the other calendar publishes for sharing, and treat it like a password.

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:03.429
Anyone who has it can read that calendar.

00:03:04.179 --> 00:03:07.381
The address must be reachable from the internet.

00:03:07.381 --> 00:03:10.759
Addresses on private or local networks are refused.

00:03:11.509 --> 00:03:14.684
To stop following a calendar, untick the box.

00:03:14.684 --> 00:03:20.409
Subscribing is one direction only, and nothing you do here changes the other calendar.

00:03:22.409 --> 00:03:27.540
Paste a calendar's address, and its events appear in yours and stay up to date.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.109
Thanks for watching.

